<at-text-block class="at-col-span-100" theme="white">

    <p>An easy climb up Mount Eden / Maungawhau, the highest volcano in Auckland. You will get spectacular views of the harbour and city.</p>
<h5>Mount Eden shops</h5>
<p>Take a 15-minute bus ride from <a href="https://at.govt.nz/bus-train-ferry/journey-planner?timeMode=Leaving+now&amp;date=2025-11-07T00%3A00%3A00%2B13%3A00&amp;time=11%3A50am&amp;transportMode=bus&amp;fareType=ADULT&amp;maxWalkingTime=10&amp;walkingSpeed=4.5&amp;routeFilter=&amp;showExternalProviders=false&amp;preferredRoute=FEWEST_TRANSFERS&amp;tab=pt&amp;fromAddress=7026+-+Commerce+Street%2FGore+Street&amp;fromCoordinates=-36.84453%2C174.76826&amp;toAddress=1870+-+Tahaki+Reserve&amp;toCoordinates=-36.87362%2C174.76224&amp;_gl=1*1ke8g9g*_gcl_au*OTk5Njc1ODA5LjE3NjExODcwNjY.*_ga*MjY5MjU0MzY1LjE3NjExODcwNjc.*_ga_WNC2W47P8Y*czE3NjI0Nzk2ODEkbzE4JGcxJHQxNzYyNDgwODMxJGoxOSRsMCRoMA..&amp;searchType=TIME_MODE" title="Commerce Street to Tahaki Reserve" data-anchor="?timeMode=Leaving+now&amp;date=2025-11-07T00%3A00%3A00%2B13%3A00&amp;time=11%3A50am&amp;transportMode=bus&amp;fareType=ADULT&amp;maxWalkingTime=10&amp;walkingSpeed=4.5&amp;routeFilter=&amp;showExternalProviders=false&amp;preferredRoute=FEWEST_TRANSFERS&amp;tab=pt&amp;fromAddress=7026+-+Commerce+Street%2FGore+Street&amp;fromCoordinates=-36.84453%2C174.76826&amp;toAddress=1870+-+Tahaki+Reserve&amp;toCoordinates=-36.87362%2C174.76224&amp;_gl=1*1ke8g9g*_gcl_au*OTk5Njc1ODA5LjE3NjExODcwNjY.*_ga*MjY5MjU0MzY1LjE3NjExODcwNjc.*_ga_WNC2W47P8Y*czE3NjI0Nzk2ODEkbzE4JGcxJHQxNzYyNDgwODMxJGoxOSRsMCRoMA..&amp;searchType=TIME_MODE">Commerce Street (7026)</a> to Tahaki Reserve stop (1870).</p>
<h5>Mount Eden summit</h5>
<p>Walk to Hillside Cresent North and up Puhi Huia Road then follow the track up Mount Eden. The walk is 2.1km long. It takes 40 minutes and you climb 3,510 steps.</p>


</at-text-block>



